WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.030
A desert floor: bare,
crusted, rocky ground,

2
00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:06.050
with little vegetation.

3
00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:08.890
Yet a channel is cut deep across it.

4
00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:12.190
It is a stream bed, and it is empty.

5
00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:15.270
Even a great river like
the Nile crosses desert,

6
00:00:15.320 --> 00:00:18.130
but its water comes from outside it.

7
00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:21.190
So if deserts are defined
by a lack of water,

8
00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:23.990
why are so many of their
landforms made by water?

9
00:00:24.040 --> 00:00:28.210
In this mission, you'll sort out
where desert water comes from,

10
00:00:28.260 --> 00:00:30.230
and when it arrives.

11
00:00:30.280 --> 00:00:34.050
Then you'll read a desert from the
mountain front down to the basin floor,

12
00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:37.610
and judge which landforms
are still forming.

13
00:00:37.660 --> 00:00:42.370
Your mission: explain why so many
desert landforms are made by water.
